FAILURE
--
N5008 [locale.general]/8 (startup global locale is the "C" locale) + C99
7.4 (the "C"-locale character classes).  libstdc++ initialises the locale
facet table inside libstdc++.so, invisible to CBMC, so every
use_facet/ctype access used to dereference nondet pointers.  CBMC now
models the classic ctype<char> facet (static classification table in the
glibc _ISbit encoding that the parsed headers give to
std::ctype_base::digit etc., plus a facet object returned by
__try_use_facet<ctype<char>>).  Positive AND negative membership checks
for digit/alpha/xdigit/space/upper/punct; runtime-verified against
g++/clang++.
